===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|nexte}}, {{m|enm|nexste}}, {{m|enm|nixte}}, from {{inh|en|ang|nīehsta}}, {{m|ang|nīehste}}, etc., inflected forms of {{m|ang|nīehst|t=nearest, next}}, superlative form of {{m|ang|nēah||nigh}} (the comparative would become {{m|en|near}}), corresponding to {{inh|en|gem-pro|*nēhwist|t=nearest, closest}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|nigh|est|nocat=1}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|stq|naist|t=next}}, {{cog|nl|naast|t=next to}}, {{cog|de|nächster|t=next}}, {{cog|yi|נעקסט|t=next}}, {{cog|da|næste|t=next}}, {{cog|ovd|nest|t=by, near}}, {{cog|is|næst|t=next}}, {{cog|nb,nn|neste|t=next}}, {{cog|sv|näst}}, {{m|sv|nästa|t=next}}, {{cog|fa|نزد|tr=nazd|t=near, with}}.

Compare typologically {{m+|la|proximus||nearest, next}}.

